From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: the mouse leaves a tracked window when another window covers the point

Purpose: end mouse tracking (TrackMouseEvent's TME_LEAVE and TME_HOVER)
when the cursor moves onto a window that covers the tracked one.
Windows behavior: WM_MOUSELEAVE comes when the cursor is no longer over
the window, whichever window it is over now (another application's
window, the taskbar over the desktop).
Wine before: the tracking timer looked for the window under the cursor
among the tracked window and its children only, so a point covered by
another top-level window still counted as inside: the leave never came,
and the tracking and hover timers ran as long as the cursor stayed over
the covering window. Windows 7's desktop icons (a list view as large as
the screen) kept its shell waking about 175 times a second, with
wineserver about 230, while the cursor was on the desktop or the
taskbar: the list view's hover kept restarting the tracking, and its
tooltip kept checking whether the cursor had left.
Change: the window under the cursor is looked for among all windows.
Evidence: Windows 7's shell in a nested session, idle with the cursor on
the desktop, on the taskbar and on the desktop again: about 175, 25 and
175 wakeups a second before, 0 after (the reference machine: 1.6 a second
on the desktop, measured with NtQuerySystemInformation's thread context
switches). Menu and toolbar hot items still end when the cursor leaves
them; the taskbar's window list still shows and hides.
---
 dlls/win32u/input.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/input.c b/dlls/win32u/input.c
index c86a357..d14baa9 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -1695,7 +1695,10 @@ static HWND get_mouse_window( HWND hwnd, INT *hittest, POINT *ret_pos, struct mo
     HWND ret;
 
     NtUserGetCursorPos( &pos );
-    ret = window_from_point( hwnd, pos, hittest, FALSE );
+    /* The window under the cursor among all windows, as Windows decides that the
+     * mouse left: a window over the tracked one (another application's, or the
+     * taskbar over the desktop's icons) is not inside it, though the point is. */
+    ret = window_from_point( 0, pos, hittest, FALSE );
     if (ret && ret == tracking->last_mouse_message_hwnd)
     {
         *hittest = tracking->last_mouse_message_hittest;
